From e8579e3001a0eb306392d3830fe7c97de1b23b69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:59:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mempool: add TigerBeetle chunked slab allocator for mapTx and
 mapNextTx

Replace individual ::operator new node allocations in CTxMemPool::mapTx (boost::multi_index_container) and CTxMemPool::mapNextTx (indirectmap) with a TigerBeetle-style ChunkedSlabAllocator<T, 16384> backed by contiguous slab chunks and an O(1) LIFO intrusive freelist.

- Add SlabArena, ChunkedSlabResource, and ChunkedSlabAllocator in src/support/allocators/chunked_slab.h, serving single-node (n == 1) allocations from 16,384-slot contiguous chunks + intrusive freelist while forwarding multi-element (n > 1) hash bucket arrays to aligned ::operator new.
- Add an optional Allocator template parameter (with automatic value_type rebinding) to indirectmap in src/indirectmap.h while preserving 100% source compatibility for 2-parameter callers.
- Wire ChunkedSlabAllocator into CTxMemPool::indexed_transaction_set (mapTx) and CTxMemPool::mapNextTx in src/txmempool.h, along with memusage::DynamicUsage overloads.
- Add mempool_slab_allocator_churn unit test in src/test/mempool_tests.cpp covering direct slab bump allocation, multi-chunk growth, LIFO freelist reuse, allocator rebinding, n > 1 fallback, and CTxMemPool churn.

Original-Commit: 4b0175724f1cd3b6c1ad69d7101e1d71bcd716bc
Original-Patch: ecash/043
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Context-only three-way application repair against the preserved repaired prefix; retain the patch additions/removals and review final endpoint diff before semantics claims.

Repair: charge retained slab chunks and separately allocated bucket arrays,
rather than multiplying live nodes by a heap-allocation estimate. On explicit
mempool clear, sweep wholly free chunks while preserving any live sentinel
chunk; allocation/free remain constant-time. Atomic batch capacity projection
includes the next slab chunk and conservative hash-table growth before any
transaction insertion. Tests cover accounting, empty/partially live release,
regrowth, and mempool churn.

